WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.400
A college student recently asked me
whether students should invest in

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.820
bitcoin. I said I don't give investment
advice, but I cautioned her: Be careful

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:17.780
what you mean by invest! You see, crypto
currencies – or coins – aren't like stocks

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:22.529
that give you rights to a company. With
most coins, all you own is the right to

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:26.039
transfer it to someone else.
She said, "That sounds like traditional

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:31.080
currencies. So why does bitcoin fluctuate
in value so much?" With traditional

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.520
currencies, when people want to do more
transactions or save more, the amount of

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.410
the currency grows (if governments are
doing their job), so the value stays about

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:45.750
the same. Not so with cryptocurrencies!
Their supply is driven by software which

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:50.760
generally creates new coin at a fixed pace,
regardless of the demand for the coin. So

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.660
whenever people want more, whether for
transactions or to speculate for future

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.800
values – or just because they're
enthusiastic about coin – the value grows.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.660
When people want less, the value drops.
It's all about demand. So with

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.360
cryptocurrencies, know what you own.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.480
Do you think cryptocurrencies are a good

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:13.650
investment? Let us know your comments.
Also, let us know what other topics you'd

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:18.930
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,
and be sure to like and subscribe for

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:23.330
more research and videos from AEI.

